=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 375.1,93.7 L 321.1,124.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 363.2 31.5 Q 363.2 25.1, 366.3 21.6 Q 369.5 18.0, 375.3 18.0 Q 381.2 18.0, 384.3 21.6 Q 387.5 25.1, 387.5 31.5 Q 387.5 37.9, 384.3 41.6 Q 381.1 45.2, 375.3 45.2 Q 369.5 45.2, 366.3 41.6 Q 363.2 37.9, 363.2 31.5 M 375.3 42.2 Q 379.4 42.2, 381.5 39.5 Q 383.7 36.8, 383.7 31.5 Q 383.7 26.3, 381.5 23.7 Q 379.4 21.0, 375.3 21.0 Q 371.3 21.0, 369.1 23.6 Q 366.9 26.3, 366.9 31.5 Q 366.9 36.8, 369.1 39.5 Q 371.3 42.2, 375.3 42.2 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 391.6 18.3 L 395.2 18.3 L 395.2 29.6 L 408.7 29.6 L 408.7 18.3 L 412.3 18.3 L 412.3 44.8 L 408.7 44.8 L 408.7 32.6 L 395.2 32.6 L 395.2 44.8 L 391.6 44.8 L 391.6 18.3 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 377.9 151.4 Q 378.6 151.4, 379.2 151.2 L 379.8 152.7 Q 378.7 153.0, 377.8 153.0 Q 376.2 153.0, 375.2 152.0 Q 374.2 151.1, 374.0 149.3 Q 371.6 149.0, 370.4 147.3 Q 369.1 145.5, 369.1 142.7 Q 369.1 139.7, 370.7 138.0 Q 372.2 136.3, 375.0 136.3 Q 377.8 136.3, 379.3 138.0 Q 380.9 139.7, 380.9 142.7 Q 380.9 145.7, 379.4 147.5 Q 378.0 149.2, 375.4 149.3 Q 375.6 150.3, 376.3 150.9 Q 377.0 151.4, 377.9 151.4 M 370.9 142.7 Q 370.9 145.3, 372.0 146.6 Q 373.1 147.9, 375.0 147.9 Q 376.9 147.9, 378.0 146.6 Q 379.1 145.3, 379.1 142.7 Q 379.1 140.2, 378.0 139.0 Q 376.9 137.7, 375.0 137.7 Q 373.1 137.7, 372.0 139.0 Q 370.9 140.2, 370.9 142.7 '' fill=''#000000''/></svg>', '["Functional group isomerism", "Chain isomerism", "Optical isomerism", "Position isomerism"]', 3, 'Both have the same three-carbon chain and the same –OH group. Only the position of –OH changes: on carbon 1 in propan-1-ol (P) and on carbon 2 in propan-2-ol (Q). That is position isomerism.', '{"0": "Both compounds are alcohols, so the functional group is the same.", "1": "The carbon chain is an unbranched three-carbon chain in both, so the chain is not what differs.", "2": "Neither has a carbon with four different groups, so neither shows optical isomerism."}', 1),
  ('CHE-2008', 'Chemistry', 'Fundamental principles of organic chemistry', 'Isomerism', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'What type of isomerism is shown by the pair of compounds below?', '<svg version=''1.1'' xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''500px'' height=''170px'' viewBox=''0 0 500 170''><path d=''M 219.4,53.4 L 156.4,89.7'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 156.4,89.7 L 93.6,53.3'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 93.6,53.3 L 30.6,89.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 159.6,87.9 L 156.4,89.7 L 153.3,87.9'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 96.7,55.1 L 93.6,53.3 L 90.4,55.1'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 124.7 140.3 Q 126.9 140.3, 128.0 141.2 Q 129.1 142.2, 129.1 144.0 Q 129.1 145.8, 127.9 146.8 Q 126.8 147.8, 124.7 147.8 L 122.7 147.8 L 122.7 153.0 L 120.9 153.0 L 120.9 140.3 L 124.7 140.3 M 124.7 146.3 Q 125.9 146.3, 126.6 145.7 Q 127.3 145.1, 127.3 144.0 Q 127.3 142.9, 126.6 142.3 Q 126.0 141.7, 124.7 141.7 L 122.7 141.7 L 122.7 146.3 L 124.7 146.3 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 375.1,17.0 L 375.0,89.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 375.0,89.6 L 437.9,126.0'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 375.0,89.6 L 312.1,125.9'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 377.9 151.4 Q 378.6 151.4, 379.2 151.2 L 379.8 152.7 Q 378.7 153.0, 377.8 153.0 Q 376.2 153.0, 375.2 152.0 Q 374.2 151.1, 374.0 149.3 Q 371.6 149.0, 370.4 147.3 Q 369.1 145.5, 369.1 142.7 Q 369.1 139.7, 370.7 138.0 Q 372.2 136.3, 375.0 136.3 Q 377.8 136.3, 379.3 138.0 Q 380.9 139.7, 380.9 142.7 Q 380.9 145.7, 379.4 147.5 Q 378.0 149.2, 375.4 149.3 Q 375.6 150.3, 376.3 150.9 Q 377.0 151.4, 377.9 151.4 M 370.9 142.7 Q 370.9 145.3, 372.0 146.6 Q 373.1 147.9, 375.0 147.9 Q 376.9 147.9, 378.0 146.6 Q 379.1 145.3, 379.1 142.7 Q 379.1 140.2, 378.0 139.0 Q 376.9 137.7, 375.0 137.7 Q 373.1 137.7, 372.0 139.0 Q 370.9 140.2, 370.9 142.7 '' fill=''#000000''/></svg>', '["Position isomerism", "Functional group isomerism", "Chain isomerism", "Geometric isomerism"]', 2, 'Both are alkanes, C₄H₁₀. Butane (P) has a straight chain of four carbons and 2-methylpropane (Q) has a branched chain of three with a methyl group. Isomers that differ in the carbon skeleton are chain isomers.', '{"0": "Alkanes have no functional group whose position could change. The skeleton itself is different.", "1": "Both are alkanes, so the functional group (class) is the same.", "3": "There is no C=C or ring to restrict rotation, so cis-trans isomerism is impossible."}', 1)
) AS s
JOIN users u ON u.email = 'hozaiphaa@gmail.com';

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions
  (id, subject, chapter, topic, difficulty, source, stem, figure, options, answer, why, wrong, mdcat, stage, free, checks, writer_id, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT s.column1, s.column2, s.column3, s.column4, s.column5, s.column6, s.column7, s.column8, s.column9, s.column10, s.column11, s.column12, s.column13,
  'live', 0, '[]', u.id, unixepoch() * 1000, unixepoch() * 1000
FROM (VALUES
  ('CHE-2009', 'Chemistry', 'Fundamental principles of organic chemistry', 'Geometric isomerism', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'What is the correct name of the alkene shown?', '<svg version=''1.1'' xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''300px'' height=''180px'' viewBox=''0 0 300 180''><path d=''M 228.4,21.6 L 228.5,112.2'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 228.5,112.2 L 150.0,157.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 214.9,104.4 L 150.0,141.9'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 150.0,157.6 L 71.5,112.4'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 228.5,107.7 L 228.5,112.2 L 224.6,114.5'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 154.0,155.3 L 150.0,157.6 L 146.1,155.3'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /></svg>', '["trans-but-2-ene", "but-1-ene", "2-methylpropene", "cis-but-2-ene"]', 3, 'The double bond is between carbons 2 and 3 of a four-carbon chain (but-2-ene). The two methyl groups are on the same side of the double bond, so it is the cis isomer.', '{"0": "In the trans isomer the two methyl groups would be on opposite sides of the C=C.", "1": "In but-1-ene the double bond is at the end of the chain, between carbons 1 and 2.", "2": "2-methylpropene has a branched chain, with both methyl groups on the same carbon of the C=C."}', 1),
