  ('CHE-2012', 'Chemistry', 'Fundamental principles of organic chemistry', 'Optical isomerism', 'hard', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'How many chiral carbon atoms does the compound shown contain?', '<svg version=''1.1'' xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''300px'' height=''180px'' viewBox=''0 0 300 180''><path d=''M 207.2,100.9 L 169.0,79.0'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 169.0,79.0 L 169.0,50.1'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 169.0,79.0 L 131.0,101.1'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 131.0,101.1 L 131.0,131.2'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 131.0,101.1 L 92.8,79.2'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 159.3 35.8 Q 159.3 29.6, 162.2 26.4 Q 165.1 23.1, 170.7 23.1 Q 175.8 23.1, 178.6 26.7 L 176.2 28.6 Q 174.2 26.0, 170.7 26.0 Q 166.9 26.0, 164.9 28.5 Q 162.9 31.0, 162.9 35.8 Q 162.9 40.8, 165.0 43.3 Q 167.1 45.8, 171.1 45.8 Q 173.8 45.8, 177.0 44.2 L 178.0 46.8 Q 176.7 47.7, 174.7 48.2 Q 172.8 48.7, 170.6 48.7 Q 165.1 48.7, 162.2 45.3 Q 159.3 42.0, 159.3 35.8 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 181.1 21.6 L 184.3 21.6 L 184.3 48.3 L 181.1 48.3 L 181.1 21.6 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 134.7 144.5 Q 137.1 145.2, 138.3 146.6 Q 139.5 148.1, 139.5 150.2 Q 139.5 153.7, 137.3 155.7 Q 135.1 157.6, 131.0 157.6 L 122.6 157.6 L 122.6 132.7 L 129.9 132.7 Q 134.2 132.7, 136.3 134.4 Q 138.5 136.1, 138.5 139.3 Q 138.5 143.1, 134.7 144.5 M 125.9 135.5 L 125.9 143.3 L 129.9 143.3 Q 132.4 143.3, 133.7 142.3 Q 135.0 141.3, 135.0 139.3 Q 135.0 135.5, 129.9 135.5 L 125.9 135.5 M 131.0 154.8 Q 133.4 154.8, 134.7 153.6 Q 136.0 152.5, 136.0 150.2 Q 136.0 148.2, 134.6 147.2 Q 133.1 146.1, 130.4 146.1 L 125.9 146.1 L 125.9 154.8 L 131.0 154.8 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 145.2 139.5 L 145.6 142.0 Q 147.5 139.2, 150.6 139.2 Q 151.6 139.2, 152.9 139.5 L 152.4 142.5 Q 150.9 142.1, 150.0 142.1 Q 148.5 142.1, 147.5 142.7 Q 146.6 143.3, 145.8 144.7 L 145.8 157.6 L 142.5 157.6 L 142.5 139.5 L 145.2 139.5 '' fill=''#000000''/></svg>', '["1", "0", "2", "4"]', 2, 'Carbon 2 carries –H, –Cl, –CH₃ and –CHBrCH₃, which are four different groups. Carbon 3 carries –H, –Br, –CH₃ and –CHClCH₃, also four different groups. The end carbons are –CH₃ groups. So there are two chiral centres in 2-bromo-3-chlorobutane.', '{"0": "Both the carbon carrying Cl and the carbon carrying Br have four different groups, not just one of them.", "1": "A carbon with four different groups is chiral, and this molecule has two of them.", "3": "The two end carbons are –CH₃ groups with three identical hydrogens, so they cannot be chiral."}', 1)
