, the least stable carbocation, so it hardly reacts by SN1. It is the fastest by SN2.", "2": "A primary carbocation is unstable, so bromoethane reacts mainly by SN2.", "3": "A secondary carbocation is less stable than a tertiary one, so it forms more slowly."}', 1),
  ('CHE-2039', 'Chemistry', 'Alkyl halides', 'SN2 reactions', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'Which of the chloroalkanes shown reacts fastest with hydroxide ions by an SN2 mechanism?', '<svg version=''1.1'' xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''760px'' height=''160px'' viewBox=''0 0 760 160''><path d=''M 66.8,35.0 L 95.1,84.2'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 95.1,84.2 L 144.1,112.7'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 95.1,84.2 L 45.9,112.5'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 95.1,84.2 L 114.8,50.3'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 114.3 36.0 Q 114.3 30.0, 117.1 26.9 Q 119.9 23.7, 125.3 23.7 Q 130.2 23.7, 132.9 27.2 L 130.6 29.1 Q 128.7 26.5, 125.3 26.5 Q 121.6 26.5, 119.7 29.0 Q 117.8 31.4, 117.8 36.0 Q 117.8 40.8, 119.7 43.2 Q 121.7 45.7, 125.6 45.7 Q 128.3 45.7, 131.4 44.1 L 132.3 46.6 Q 131.1 47.5, 129.2 47.9 Q 127.3 48.4, 125.2 48.4 Q 119.9 48.4, 117.1 45.2 Q 114.3 42.0, 114.3 36.0 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 135.3 22.3 L 138.5 22.3 L 138.5 48.1 L 135.3 48.1 L 135.3 22.3 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 94.7 131.3 Q 96.9 131.3, 98.0 132.2 Q 99.1 133.2, 99.1 135.0 Q 99.1 136.8, 97.9 137.8 Q 96.8 138.8, 94.7 138.8 L 92.7 138.8 L 92.7 144.0 L 90.9 144.0 L 90.9 131.3 L 94.7 131.3 M 94.7 137.3 Q 95.9 137.3, 96.6 136.7 Q 97.3 136.1, 97.3 135.0 Q 97.3 133.9, 96.6 133.3 Q 96.0 132.7, 94.7 132.7 L 92.7 132.7 L 92.7 137.3 L 94.7 137.3 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 334.1,116.6 L 285.1,88.1'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 285.1,88.1 L 235.9,116.2'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 285.1,88.1 L 285.3,46.4'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 276.0 32.2 Q 276.0 26.2, 278.8 23.0 Q 281.6 19.9, 287.0 19.9 Q 291.9 19.9, 294.6 23.4 L 292.4 25.2 Q 290.4 22.7, 287.0 22.7 Q 283.3 22.7, 281.4 25.1 Q 279.5 