 665.0,84.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 701.2,105.3 L 703.1,106.4 L 705.0,105.3'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 739.1,85.4 L 741.0,84.3 L 741.0,82.1'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 740.8,42.6 L 740.8,40.4 L 738.9,39.3'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 704.7,19.7 L 702.8,18.6 L 700.9,19.7'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 666.7,39.6 L 664.8,40.7 L 664.8,42.9'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 618.5 106.7 Q 618.5 102.2, 620.7 99.7 Q 622.9 97.2, 627.1 97.2 Q 631.2 97.2, 633.4 99.7 Q 635.6 102.2, 635.6 106.7 Q 635.6 111.2, 633.4 113.8 Q 631.2 116.4, 627.1 116.4 Q 623.0 116.4, 620.7 113.8 Q 618.5 111.3, 618.5 106.7 M 627.1 114.3 Q 629.9 114.3, 631.4 112.4 Q 633.0 110.4, 633.0 106.7 Q 633.0 103.1, 631.4 101.2 Q 629.9 99.3, 627.1 99.3 Q 624.2 99.3, 622.7 101.2 Q 621.2 103.0, 621.2 106.7 Q 621.2 110.5, 622.7 112.4 Q 624.2 114.3, 627.1 114.3 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 661.4 141.7 Q 661.5 141.7, 662.1 142.0 Q 662.7 142.2, 663.4 142.4 Q 664.0 142.5, 664.7 142.5 Q 665.9 142.5, 666.6 142.0 Q 667.3 141.4, 667.3 140.3 Q 667.3 139.6, 666.9 139.2 Q 666.6 138.8, 666.1 138.5 Q 665.5 138.3, 664.6 138.0 Q 663.5 137.7, 662.8 137.4 Q 662.1 137.1, 661.7 136.4 Q 661.2 135.7, 661.2 134.5 Q 661.2 132.9, 662.3 131.9 Q 663.4 131.0, 665.5 131.0 Q 667.0 131.0, 668.7 131.7 L 668.3 133.0 Q 666.7 132.4, 665.6 132.4 Q 664.3 132.4, 663.6 132.9 Q 663.0 133.4, 663.0 134.3 Q 663.0 135.0, 663.3 135.4 Q 663.7 135.8, 664.2 136.1 Q 664.7 136.3, 665.6 136.6 Q 666.7 136.9, 667.4 137.3 Q 668.1 137.6, 668.6 138.4 Q 669.1 139.1, 669.1 140.3 Q 669.1 142.1, 667.9 143.1 Q 666.7 144.0, 664.8 144.0 Q 663.6 144.0, 662.8 143.7 Q 661.9 143.5, 660.9 143.1 L 661.4 141.7 '' fill=''#000000''/></svg>', '["P", "Q", "R", "S"]', 1, 'Phenol (Q) is a weak acid. Its anion is stabilised because the negative charge spreads into the benzene ring, so phenol reacts with NaOH to form sodium phenoxide. Alcohols such as ethanol and cyclohexanol are far weaker acids and do not react with aqueous NaOH, and methoxybenzene has no O–H at all.', '{"0": "Ethanol is a weaker acid than water and does not form a salt with aqueous NaOH.", "2": "In cyclohexanol the –OH is on a saturated ring, so its anion has no ring to spread the charge into.", "3": "Methoxybenzene is an ether with no acidic hydrogen on oxygen."}', 1),
  ('CHE-2050', 'Chemistry', 'Alcohols and phenols', 'Preparation of ethers', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'Which pair of reagents can be used to make the ether shown?', '<svg version=''1.1'' xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''300px'' height=''180px'' viewBox=''0 0 300 180''><path d=''M 264.0,104.1 L 188.0,60.2'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 188.0,60.2 L 127.9,95.0'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 96.1,95.0 L 36.0,60.4'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 191.8,62.4 L 188.0,60.2 L 185.0,62.0'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 99.0 104.3 Q 99.0 97.5, 102.4 93.7 Q 105.7 89.9, 112.0 89.9 Q 118.3 89.9, 121.7 93.7 Q 125.0 97.5, 125.0 104.3 Q 125.0 111.2, 121.6 115.1 Q 118.2 119.0, 112.0 119.0 Q 105.8 119.0, 102.4 115.1 Q 99.0 111.2, 99.0 104.3 M 112.0 115.8 Q 116.3 115.8, 118.7 112.9 Q 121.0 110.0, 121.0 104.3 Q 121.0 98.7, 118.7 95.9 Q 116.3 93.1, 112.0 93.1 Q 107.7 93.1, 105.3 95.9 Q 103.0 98.7, 103.0 104.3 Q 103.0 110.0, 105.3 112.9 Q 107.7 115.8, 112.0 115.8 '' fill=''#000000''/></svg>', '["Sodium ethoxide and iodomethane", "Ethanol and methanol at room temperature", "Ethene and methanol at room temperature", "Ethanal and methanol"]', 0, 'The compound is methoxyethane, CH₃CH₂–O–CH₃. In the Williamson synthesis an alkoxide ion attacks an alkyl halide: CH₃CH₂O⁻Na⁺ + CH₃I → CH₃CH₂OCH₃ + NaI.', '{"1": "Two alcohols do not join to form an ether at room temperature without an acid catalyst.", "2": "Ethene and methanol do not react at room temperature without a catalyst.", "3": "Ethanal and methanol give a hemiacetal or acetal, which is not this simple ether."}', 1),
  ('CHE-2051', 'Chemistry', 'Aldehydes, ketones and carboxylic acids', 'Naming aldehydes', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'What is the IUPAC name of the compound shown?', '<svg version=''1.1'' xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''300px'' height=''180px'' viewBox=''0 0 300 180''><path d=''M 37.3,135.9 L 90.9,105.0'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 90.9,105.0 L 91.0,43.2'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 90.9,105.0 L 144.5,136.0'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 144.5,136.0 L 198.1,105.1'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 202.7,107.8 L 202.7,60.1'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 193.4,107.8 L 193.5,60.1'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 198.1,105.1 L 238.5,128.5'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 141.8,134.5 L 144.5,136.0 L 147.1,134.5'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 195.4,106.7 L 198.1,105.1 L 200.1,106.3'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 185.1 43.3 Q 185.1 36.5, 188.5 32.7 Q 191.8 28.9, 198.1 28.9 Q 204.4 28.9, 207.7 32.7 Q 211.1 36.5, 211.1 43.3 Q 211.1 50.2, 207.7 54.1 Q 204.3 58.0, 198.1 58.0 Q 191.9 58.0, 188.5 54.1 Q 185.1 50.3, 185.1 43.3 M 198.1 54.8 Q 202.4 54.8, 204.7 51.9 Q 207.1 49.0, 207.1 43.3 Q 207.1 37.8, 204.7 35.0 Q 202.4 32.1, 198.1 32.1 Q 193.8 32.1, 191.4 34.9 Q 189.1 37.7, 189.1 43.3 Q 189.1 49.1, 191.4 51.9 Q 193.8 54.8, 198.1 54.8 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 240.5 121.9 L 244.4 121.9 L 244.4 134.0 L 258.8 134.0 L 258.8 121.9 L 262.7 121.9 L 262.7 150.3 L 258.8 150.3 L 258.8 137.2 L 244.4 137.2 L 244.4 150.3 L 240.5 150.3 L 240.5 121.9 '' fill=''#000000''/></svg>', '["2-methylbutanal", "3-methylbutan-1-one", "3-methylbutanal", "2-methylbutan-4-al"]', 2, 'The –CHO carbon is always carbon 1. The chain has four carbons (butanal), and the methyl group is on carbon 3: 3-methylbutanal.', '{"0": "Counting from the –CHO carbon, the methyl group is on C3, not C2.", "1": "The suffix -one is for ketones. A C=O at the end of a chain is an aldehyde (-al).", "3": "The aldehyde carbon must be C1, so numbering starts there."}', 1),
  ('CHE-2052', 'Chemistry', 'Aldehydes, ketones and carboxylic acids', 'Naming ketones', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'What is the IUPAC name of the compound shown?', '<svg version=''1.1'' xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''300px'' height=''180px'' viewBox=''0 0 300 180''><path d=''M 65.5,84.3 L 107.7,108.7'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 107.7,108.7 L 150.0,84.4'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 153.7,86.5 L 153.7,51.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 146.3,86.5 L 146.4,51.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 150.0,84.4 L 192.2,108.8'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 192.2,108.8 L 234.5,84.4'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 192.2,108.8 L 192.2,157.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 105.6,107.5 L 107.7,108.7 L 109.8,107.5'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 147.9,85.6 L 150.0,84.4 L 152.1,85.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 137.4 35.7 Q 137.4 29.0, 140.6 25.3 Q 143.9 21.6, 150.0 21.6 Q 156.2 21.6, 159.4 25.3 Q 162.7 29.0, 162.7 35.7 Q 162.7 42.4, 159.4 46.2 Q 156.1 50.0, 150.0 50.0 Q 143.9 50.0, 140.6 46.2 Q 137.4 42.4, 137.4 35.7 M 150.0 46.9 Q 154.3 46.9, 156.5 44.0 Q 158.8 41.2, 158.8 35.7 Q 158.8 30.2, 156.5 27.5 Q 154.3 24.7, 150.0 24.7 Q 145.8 24.7, 143.5 27.5 Q 141.3 30.2, 141.3 35.7 Q 141.3 41.2, 143.5 44.0 Q 145.8 46.9, 150.0 46.9 '' fill=''#000000''/></svg>', '["4-methylpentan-3-one", "2-methylpentan-2-one", "Hexan-3-one", "2-methylpentan-3-one"]', 3, 'The chain has five carbons, and the C=O is on C3 from either end. The methyl group then decides the numbering: it gets the lower number, 2, giving 2-methylpentan-3-one.', '{"0": "When the C=O gets 3 from both ends, number so that the methyl group gets the lower locant, 2.", "1": "The C=O is on the third carbon, not the second.", "2": "The chain has five carbons with a methyl branch, not six in a row."}', 1)
) AS s
JOIN users u ON u.email = 'hozaiphaa@gmail.com';

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions
  (id, subject, chapter, topic, difficulty, source, stem, figure, options, answer, why, wrong, mdcat, stage, free, checks, writer_id, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT s.column1, s.column2, s.column3, s.column4, s.column5, s.column6, s.column7, s.column8, s.column9, s.column10, s.column11, s.column12, s.column13,
