y on the C=O. Pentan-3-one has ethyl groups on both sides, propanal has CH₃CH₂CO–, and propan-1-ol gives propanal.', '{"0": "Pentan-3-one has –CH₂CH₃ on each side of the C=O, so it has no CH₃CO– group.", "2": "Propanal is CH₃CH₂CHO. Its carbonyl has an ethyl group and an H, not a methyl group.", "3": "Propan-1-ol is oxidised to propanal, which has no CH₃CO– group."}', 1),
