h makes it the least reactive here."}', 1),
  ('CHE-2059', 'Chemistry', 'Aldehydes, ketones and carboxylic acids', 'Naming carboxylic acids', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'What is the IUPAC name of the compound shown?', '<svg version=''1.1'' xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''300px'' height=''180px'' viewBox=''0 0 300 180''><path d=''M 177.3,21.6 L 177.4,70.2'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 177.4,70.2 L 219.5,94.5'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 177.4,70.2 L 135.3,94.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 138.9,92.5 L 109.2,75.4'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 135.3,98.8 L 105.6,81.7'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 135.3,94.6 L 135.4,127.7'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 137.4,93.4 L 135.3,94.6 L 135.3,96.3'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 80.5 70.5 Q 80.5 63.9, 83.8 60.2 Q 87.0 56.5, 93.1 56.5 Q 99.2 56.5, 102.5 60.2 Q 105.8 63.9, 105.8 70.5 Q 105.8 77.2, 102.5 81.0 Q 99.2 84.7, 93.1 84.7 Q 87.1 84.7, 83.8 81.0 Q 80.5 77.2, 80.5 70.5 M 93.1 81.6 Q 97.3 81.6, 99.6 78.8 Q 101.9 76.0, 101.9 70.5 Q 101.9 65.1, 99.6 62.3 Q 97.3 59.6, 93.1 59.6 Q 88.9 59.6, 86.6 62.3 Q 84.4 65.0, 84.4 70.5 Q 84.4 76.0, 86.6 78.8 Q 88.9 81.6, 93.1 81.6 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 122.7 143.3 Q 122.7 136.7, 126.0 133.0 Q 129.3 129.3, 135.4 129.3 Q 141.5 129.3, 144.8 133.0 Q 148.0 136.7, 148.0 143.3 Q 148.0 150.0, 144.7 153.8 Q 141.4 157.6, 135.4 157.6 Q 129.3 157.6, 126.0 153.8 Q 122.7 150.1, 122.7 143.3 M 135.4 154.5 Q 139.6 154.5, 141.9 151.7 Q 144.1 148.8, 144.1 143.3 Q 144.1 137.9, 141.9 135.2 Q 139.6 132.4, 135.4 132.4 Q 131.2 132.4, 128.9 135.2 Q 126.6 137.9, 126.6 143.3 Q 126.6 148.9, 128.9 151.7 Q 131.2 154.5, 135.4 154.5 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 152.3 129.6 L 156.1 129.6 L 156.1 141.3 L 170.1 141.3 L 170.1