  ('CHE-2063', 'Chemistry', 'Aldehydes, ketones and carboxylic acids', 'Acyl chlorides', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'The acid shown is warmed with thionyl chloride (SOCl₂). What is the organic product?', '<svg version=''1.1'' xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''300px'' height=''180px'' viewBox=''0 0 300 180''><path d=''M 73.7,138.0 L 130.3,105.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 135.2,108.4 L 135.4,57.3'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 125.4,108.4 L 125.6,57.2'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 130.3,105.6 L 171.6,129.6'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;'' /><path d=''M 127.5,107.2 L 130.3,105.6 L 132.4,106.8'' style=''fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-width:2.0px;stroke-miterlimit:10;'' /><path d=''M 117.6 40.4 Q 117.6 33.6, 120.9 29.8 Q 124.3 26.0, 130.6 26.0 Q 136.8 26.0, 140.2 29.8 Q 143.6 33.6, 143.6 40.4 Q 143.6 47.3, 140.2 51.2 Q 136.8 55.1, 130.6 55.1 Q 124.3 55.1, 120.9 51.2 Q 117.6 47.4, 117.6 40.4 M 130.6 51.9 Q 134.9 51.9, 137.2 49.0 Q 139.6 46.1, 139.6 40.4 Q 139.6 34.9, 137.2 32.1 Q 134.9 29.2, 130.6 29.2 Q 126.2 29.2, 123.9 32.0 Q 121.6 34.8, 121.6 40.4 Q 121.6 46.2, 123.9 49.0 Q 126.2 51.9, 130.6 51.9 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 173.7 138.5 Q 173.7 131.7, 177.1 127.9 Q 180.4 124.1, 186.7 124.1 Q 193.0 124.1, 196.4 127.9 Q 199.7 131.7, 199.7 138.5 Q 199.7 145.4, 196.3 149.3 Q 192.9 153.2, 186.7 153.2 Q 180.5 153.2, 177.1 149.3 Q 173.7 145.4, 173.7 138.5 M 186.7 150.0 Q 191.0 150.0, 193.4 147.1 Q 195.7 144.2, 195.7 138.5 Q 195.7 132.9, 193.4 130.1 Q 191.0 127.3, 186.7 127.3 Q 182.4 127.3, 180.0 130.1 Q 177.7 132.9, 177.7 138.5 Q 177.7 144.2, 180.0 147.1 Q 182.4 150.0, 186.7 150.0 '' fill=''#000000''/><path d=''M 204.1 124.4 L 208.0 124.4 L 208.0 136.4 L 222.4 136.4 L 222.4 124.4 L 226.3 124.4 L 226.3 152.7 L 222.4 152.7 L 222.4 139.6 L 208.0 139.6 L 208.0 152.7 L 204.1 152.7 L 204.1 124.4 '' f