  ('PHY-2001', 'Physics', 'Force and motion', 'Velocity–time graphs', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'The graph shows how the velocity of a car changes with time. How far does the car travel in the 10 s shown?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''420'' height=''260'' viewBox=''0 0 420 260''><line x1=''58.0'' y1=''214.0'' x2=''408.0'' y2=''214.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><polygon points=''400.6,217.1 408.0,214.0 400.6,210.9'' fill=''#000'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''58.0'' y1=''214.0'' x2=''58.0'' y2=''12.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><polygon points=''61.1,19.4 58.0,12.0 54.9,19.4'' fill=''#000'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''119.5'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''119.5'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''119.5'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>2</text><line x1=''180.9'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''180.9'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''180.9'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>4</text><line x1=''242.4'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''242.4'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''242.4'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>6</text><line x1=''303.8'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''303.8'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''303.8'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' f