  ('PHY-2003', 'Physics', 'Force and motion', 'Displacement–time graphs', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'The displacement–time graph of a cyclist has three parts, P, Q and R. During which part is the cyclist at rest?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''420'' height=''260'' viewBox=''0 0 420 260''><line x1=''58.0'' y1=''214.0'' x2=''408.0'' y2=''214.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><polygon points=''400.6,217.1 408.0,214.0 400.6,210.9'' fill=''#000'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''58.0'' y1=''214.0'' x2=''58.0'' y2=''12.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><polygon points=''61.1,19.4 58.0,12.0 54.9,19.4'' fill=''#000'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''100.2'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''100.2'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''100.2'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>1</text><line x1=''142.5'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''142.5'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''142.5'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>2</text><line x1=''184.8'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''184.8'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''184.8'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>3</text><line x1=''227.0'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''227.0'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''227.0'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle