erif'' font-size=''18'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>+</text><circle cx=''250.0'' cy=''110.0'' r=''13.0'' fill=''#fff'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''250.0'' y=''111.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''18'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>+</text></svg>', '["The electric field there is zero", "The electric field there is at its strongest", "The field there points towards the left charge", "The charges have opposite signs"]', 0, 'The two charges are both positive and equal. At the midpoint their fields are equal in size and opposite in direction, so they cancel. This is a neutral point, and no field lines pass through it.', '{"1": "The field is strongest close to each charge, not at the neutral point between like charges.", "2": "The fields of the two charges cancel exactly at the midpoint, so there is no field direction there.", "3": "Lines repel each other between the charges, which shows like charges."}', 1),
