<line x1=''289.0'' y1=''171.0'' x2=''301.0'' y2=''159.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''205.0'' x2=''120.0'' y2=''205.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><polygon points=''110.8,208.9 120.0,205.0 110.8,201.1'' fill=''#000'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.4'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><circle cx=''20.0'' cy=''205.0'' r=''8.0'' fill=''#fff'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''20.0'' y=''206.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''14'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>+</text><text x=''70.0'' y=''222.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''14'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-style=''italic''>v</text><text x=''300.0'' y=''205.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''12'' text-anchor=''end'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>B into page</text></svg>', '["A circle, curving downwards (clockwise)", "A straight line", "A parabola, like a projectile", "A circle, curving upwards (anticlockwise)"]', 3, 'The force is F = qv × B. With v to the right and B into the page, v × B points up the page, and q is positive, so the force is upwards. The force is always at right angles to the velocity, so the charge moves in a circle that bends upwards, going anticlockwise.', '{"0": "That would be the path of a negative charge, which feels the force in the opposite direction.", "1": "The velocity is at right angles to B, so there is a force and the path bends.", "2": "The magnetic force is always at right angles to the velocity and keeps the speed constant, which gives a circle, not a parabola."}', 1),
  ('PHY-2019', 'Physics', 'Electromagnetic induction', 'Lenz''s law', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'The north pole of a magnet is pushed into the end P of a coil, as shown. What does end P of the coil become while the magnet moves in?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''440'' height=''160'' viewBox=''0 0 440 160''><rect x=''20'' y=''60'' width=''120'' height=''40'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><line x1=''80.0'' y1=''60.0'' x2=''80.0'' y2=''100.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''50.0'' y=''81.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''16'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>S</text><text x=''110.0'' y=''81.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''16'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>N</text><line x1=''150.0'' y1=''80.0'' x2=''200.0'' y2=''80.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><polygon points=''190.8,83.9 200.0,80.0 190.8,76.1'' fill=''#000'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''175.0'' y=''64.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''12'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>moves in</text><path d=''M 230 45 C 244 45 244 115 230 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 230 45 C 222 45 222 115 230 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 252 45 C 266 45 266 115 252 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 252 45 C 244 45 244 115 252 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 274 45 C 288 45 288 115 274 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 274 45 C 266 45 266 115 274 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 296 45 C 310 45 310 115 296 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 296 45 C 288 45 288 115 296 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 318 45 C 332 45 332 115 318 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 318 45 C 310 45 310 115 318 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 340 45 C 354 45 354 115 340 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 340 45 C 332 45 332 115 340 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 362 45 C 376 45 376 115 362 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 362 45 C 354 45 354 115 362 115'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''300.0'' y=''140.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>coil</text><text x=''225.0'' y=''30.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''14'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>P</text><text x=''375.0'' y=''30.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''14'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>Q</text></svg>', '["A north pole, which repels the magnet", "A south pole, which attracts the magnet", "No pole, because no current flows", "A north pole, which attracts the magnet"]', 0, 'By Lenz''s law the induced current opposes the change that causes it. To oppose the approaching north pole, end P becomes a north pole and pushes back on the magnet. Work must be done to push the magnet in, and that work becomes electrical energy.', '{"1": "An attracting pole would help the motion and create energy from nothing, which breaks conservation of energy.", "2": "The flux through the coil is changing, so an e.m.f. is induced and a current flows in the closed coil.", "3": "Two north poles repel. They never attract."}', 1)
) AS s
JOIN users u ON u.email = 'hozaiphaa@gmail.com';

