  ('PHY-2020', 'Physics', 'Electromagnetic induction', 'Transformers', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'An ideal transformer has 400 turns on its primary coil and 100 turns on its secondary coil, as shown. The primary is connected to 240 V a.c. What is the output voltage?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''380'' height=''200'' viewBox=''0 0 380 200''><rect x=''120'' y=''30'' width=''140'' height=''140'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''3''/><rect x=''150'' y=''60'' width=''80'' height=''80'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''3''/><path d=''M 100 50 C 140 50 140 64 100 64'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 280 50 C 240 50 240 64 280 64'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 100 72 C 140 72 140 86 100 86'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 280 72 C 240 72 240 86 280 86'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 100 94 C 140 94 140 108 100 108'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 280 94 C 240 94 240 108 280 108'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 100 116 C 140 116 140 130 100 130'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 280 116 C 240 116 240 130 280 130'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 100 138 C 140 138 140 152 100 152'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><path d=''M 280 138 C 240 138 240 152 280 152'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''70.0'' y=''100.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>400 turns</text><text x=''310.0'' y=''100.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>100 turns</text><text x=''70.0'' y=''175.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>240 V a.c.</text><text x=''310.0'' y=''175.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>output</text></svg>', '["960 V", "60 V", "240 V", "24 V"]', 1, 'For an ideal transformer Vs ÷ Vp = Ns ÷ Np, so Vs = 240 × 100 ÷ 400 = 60 V. With fewer secondary turns it is a step-down transformer.', '{"0": "This uses the turns ratio upside down. 960 V would need more secondary turns.", "2": "The voltage changes because the two coils have different numbers of turns.", "3": "This divides by 10 instead of by the turns ratio of 4."}', 1),
