  ('PHY-2028', 'Physics', 'Circular motion', 'Circular motion and SHM', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'Point P moves round the circle at a steady angular speed. N is the foot of the perpendicular from P to the diameter. How does N move?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''320'' height=''260'' viewBox=''0 0 320 260''><circle cx=''150.0'' cy=''130.0'' r=''90.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><line x1=''40.0'' y1=''130.0'' x2=''260.0'' y2=''130.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round'' stroke-dasharray=''5 4''/><circle cx=''207.9'' cy=''61.1'' r=''6'' fill=''#000''/><line x1=''207.9'' y1=''61.1'' x2=''207.9'' y2=''130.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round'' stroke-dasharray=''4 4''/><circle cx=''207.9'' cy=''130.0'' r=''4'' fill=''#000''/><line x1=''150.0'' y1=''130.0'' x2=''207.9'' y2=''61.1'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''219.9'' y=''53.1'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''14'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>P</text><text x=''207.9'' y=''146.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''14'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>N</text><text x=''140.0'' y=''144.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''14'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>O</text><path d=''M 180 130 A 30 30 0 0 0 169.3 107.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''194.0'' y=''116.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''14'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-style=''italic''>θ</text></svg>', '["N moves with simple harmonic motion along the diameter", "N moves at a steady speed along the diameter", "N stays at rest at the centre O", "N moves round the circle with P"]', 0, 'As P goes round, N goes back and forth along the diameter. Its displacement from O is r cos θ, which changes sinusoidally with time, so N''s motion is simple harmonic. N is fastest at O and stops at the ends.', '{"1": "N slows down near the ends of the diameter and speeds up through O, so its speed is not steady.", "2": "N moves along the diameter as P goes round.", "3": "N is the projection of P onto the diameter. It stays on that line."}', 1),
  ('PHY-2029', 'Physics', 'Modern and nuclear physics', 'Half-life', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'The graph shows the count rate from a radioactive sample. What is the half-life of the sample?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''420'' height=''260'' viewBox=''0 0 420 260''><line x1=''58.0'' y1=''214.0'' x2=''408.0'' y2=''214.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><polygon points=''400.6,217.1 408.0,214.0 400.6,210.9'' fill=''#000'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''58.0'' y1=''214.0'' x2=''58.0'' y2=''12.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><polygon points=''61.1,19.4 58.0,12.0 54.9,19.4'' fill=''#000'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.6'' stroke-linejoin=''round'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''139.1'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''139.1'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''139.1'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>3</text><line x1=''220.2'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''220.2'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''220.2'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>6</text><line x1=''301.4'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''301.4'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''301.4'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>9</text><line x1=''382.5'' y1=''210.0'' x2=''382.5'' y2=''218.0'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.4'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><text x=''382.5'' y=''230.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''13'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000''>12</t